# Route guides maintenance

Whenever you **implement or materially change** a page, section, or feature, update the matching guide under **`docs/guides/routes/`** in the **same change** — not as a follow-up.

## Which file to update

Mirror the app URL (omit dynamic params). **Authoritative index:** [`docs/guides/routes/README.md`](../../docs/guides/routes/README.md) — do not maintain a second route→file table here.

Examples of the convention:

| Route pattern                              | Guide location                                             |
| ------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
| `/org/:orgSlug/...`                        | `docs/guides/routes/org/...`                               |
| `/org/:orgSlug/property/:propertySlug/...` | `docs/guides/routes/org/property/...`                      |
| `/org/:orgSlug/parking/:parkingSlug/...`   | `docs/guides/routes/org/parking/...`                       |
| `/admin/...`                               | `docs/guides/routes/admin/...`                             |
| `/account/...`                             | `docs/guides/routes/account/...`                           |
| Public marketing / guest operational       | top-level or nested under `docs/guides/routes/` per README |

Workflow: **`.cursor/skills/route-guides/SKILL.md`**.

## What to document

Per page/section: **behavior**, **save paths**, **validation**, **API/edge functions**, **DB/storage columns**, **permissions**, **edge cases**, **implementation map** (UI + server paths), and **Host-facing knowledge** (plain-language summary + common host Q&A — no code, DB columns, or internal endpoint names).

Update the **Progress overview** table when section status changes. Mark guide **Status** from `Pending` → `Documented` when substantive.

## Relationship to other docs

| Doc                                          | Role                                                                  |
| -------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **`docs/guides/routes/*.md`**                | Per-route behavior spec (operator + agent reference)                  |
| **`docs/PROJECT.md`**                        | Architecture, API inventory, env vars                                 |
| **`.cursor/rules/*.mdc`**                    | Canonical invariants (booking workflow, auth) — link, don't duplicate |
| **`docs/archive/planning/NEW_FLOW_PLAN.md`** | Redesign plan / decisions                                             |

New route → create guide from **`docs/guides/_template.md`**, add row to **`docs/guides/routes/README.md`**.

## When guides need no change

Typos, internal renames with no behavior change, or pure refactors that don't alter UX/API/validation.
